        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Real clip = target",
          "rect": [
            190,
            376,
            580,
            34
          ],
          "size": 24,
          "color": "#000000"
        }
      ],
      "speech": "So we train a model, and the problem is data. You'd want pairs of videos with the same content and different motion, and those don't exist, so we make them. Start with a real video, this guy walking, and cut a clip out of it. That real clip is the target, what the model has to output. The target is always real, so the model learns to output real-looking video."
    },
