        {
          "kind": "text",
          "text": "Fake in, real out",
          "rect": [
            24,
            410,
            440,
            50
          ],
          "size": 32,
          "color": "#C00000"
        }
      ],
      "speech": "Then we make a fake version with different motion. That's a motion counterfactual. Two ways. Top right, a video model fills in between two real frames. Or we resample the real frames, faster, slower, reversed, so those pairs are real frames on both sides. Then crop and zoom on all of them, bottom right. To match points, we run one tracker and start points only on real frames both videos contain. For a generated clip, that's its two real end frames. So each dot should be the same physical point, as far as the tracker gets it right. Fake video and tracks in, real video out."
    },
