      ],
      "speech": "At test time: a guy roasting a marshmallow next to a sleeping dog. I click points, a tracker follows them, and those are the source tracks. I drag them where I want them, and those are the target tracks, in the red box. The lines are just a visualization. The model actually gets each track as colored dots on black, one color per point, plus your video. It's a frozen CogVideoX, plus a trained copy of its first eighteen blocks, added back through zero-initialized layers. The target tracks line up with the output, like a normal ControlNet input. Your video doesn't. We think it works because these blocks attend across all frames. We didn't ablate that."
