      ],
      "speech": "User study: 41 people, pick the best of four, on 20 edits we chose ourselves, so there's selection bias. Ours got 69%, ATI 25, even on a stronger base model. For reconstruction, we cut each video at the middle. One half, reversed, is the input, the other half is the target, and both start on the middle frame, so image-to-video methods get a fair first frame. Reversal's in our training data, so this tests keeping content, not editing in general. SSIM is suspiciously low for every method, so I'm re-checking that eval. No error bars. Limits are on the right. We trained on 1 to 64 points, yet past about twenty it stops following. We don't know why. And pixel-perfect points make it copy the input. This is CVPR 2026, code's not out."
